prior_sd": 5.34, "poll_margin": 23.39, "poll_sd": 5.06, "poll_weight": 0.53, "fundamentals": {"margin": 7.45, "lean": -0.75, "environment": 4.2, "incumbency": 4.0, "money": 0.0}, "rating_margin": 16.0, "sigma_race": 5.0, "sigma_total": 5.46, "baseline_margin": 18.27, "analyst_adjustment": 2.73, "key_factors": ["Shapiro leads polls by roughly 20-25 points, including high-quality Quinnipiac and Siena surveys", "All seven expert raters call the race Solid or Safe D", "Prediction markets price Shapiro at 96-97%", "Incumbent advantage in a state that only leans slightly Republican"], "rationale": "Every recent poll shows Shapiro ahead by double digits, with the latest Quinnipiac and Siena surveys at 20-25 points, and raters and markets unanimously treat the race as out of reach for Garrity. The forecast lands near the polling average, tempered slightly toward the fundamentals-based view of a smaller but still decisive incumbent lead.", "watch": "A major late-breaking scandal or external shock could narrow the margin, though nothing in current evidence suggests a competitive race.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Josh Shapiro (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Pennsylvania's governor race pairs first-term incumbent Josh Shapiro against state Senator Stacy Garrity, with the state's partisan lean only slightly Republican. Polling has been remarkably consistent all cycle: every survey since June shows Shapiro ahead, with the most recent Quinnipiac poll giving him a 25-point lead and Siena and Susquehanna showing margins of roughly 20 points. Averages across aggregators put the race near 23 points.\n\nAll seven expert raters rate the race Solid or Safe Democratic, and prediction markets on Kalshi, Polymarket, and PredictIt price Shapiro's chances at 96-97%. The October debate produced no evident shift, and an Obama endorsement added to Shapiro's visibility. Garrity has struggled to close a gap that has persisted through the entire campaign, and the evidence points to a decisive incumbent win.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9929, "margin": 15.66}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9928, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9978, "margin": 19.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9956, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9951, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.995, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.995, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9972, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9889, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9946, "margin": 18.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.995, "margin": 17.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9958, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9964, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9963, "margin": 18.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9934, "margin": 17.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9971, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9988, "margin": 22.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.9983, "margin": 21.0}]}